  "releaseNotes": "**DI002 Executable-Root Coverage**: Scoped-service escape analysis now runs across constructors, accessors, local functions, lambdas, and anonymous methods instead of only ordinary methods, while still keeping escape tracking local to the current executable boundary. | **DI004 Executable-Root Coverage**: Use-after-dispose analysis now follows the same broader executable-root set, including constructor and accessor bodies plus local and anonymous functions, without speculating across nested executable boundaries. | **DI002/DI004 Regression Guardrails**: Added direct should-report and should-not-report coverage for constructor, property-getter, local-function, anonymous-method, and nested-boundary cases so the widened entry surface stays conservative.",
